WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.500
Whole numbers bigger than one are made

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.990
by multiplying primes.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.790
A prime has exactly two positive factors,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.150
one and itself.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.170
Take sixty.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.230
Split it into six and ten, then split those again.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.950
The prime pieces are two, three, two and five.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:18.930
Start another way.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.490
Write sixty as four times fifteen.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.840
Four gives two twos, and fifteen gives a three

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:25.590
and a five.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.920
Rearrange the pieces in increasing order and both trees

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.070
give the same list.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.560
That fixed prime factorisation is why we can work

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.230
with the pieces.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.510
Is ninety-one prime?

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.350
Decide which small primes you would try first,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.890
and think about how far the search needs to go.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.230
Ninety-one is odd, so two fails.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.130
Its digits add to ten, so three fails.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.110
Its last digit is one, so five fails.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.270
Try seven.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.990
Seven times thirteen equals ninety-one.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.370
These two factors show that ninety-one is composite.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.810
If both factors were bigger than the square root,

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.870
multiplying them would give too much.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.660
So a composite number has a prime factor at or below

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.730
its square root.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.010
For ninety-seven that root lies between nine and ten.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.660
Try two, three, five and seven.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.030
All leave a remainder, so ninety-seven is prime.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.660
Three different whole numbers, each bigger than one,

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.020
multiply to sixty-six.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:27.900
Which numbers are they?

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:31.490
Sixty-six has exactly three prime pieces, two,

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:32.380
three and eleven.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:34.840
Each of the three numbers needs a piece.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:38.070
Each gets exactly one, so those three primes

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:38.820
are the answer.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.520
Split a number until all its pieces are prime.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:45.690
When you test whether a number is prime, use the small

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.480
primes up to its square root.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.000
One has only one positive factor.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.790
In your notebook, write eighty-four as a

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:53.920
product of primes.
